# shell: desktop
# The moments that sound are preferences: a row per moment with its
# on/off, the sound it plays and a Test button, and one volume under
# them.  A file dropped in the sounds folder is offered beside the baked
# sound and chosen by pressing the row's name.  A press applies
# at once and is written to the settings file as a sound.<event> line;
# Test sounds a moment whether or not its row is on; Revert puts back
# what the window opened on.  A scripted run is mute, so the shell's own
# word on each moment is the proof.
wait 15
key w ctrl
wait 5
note a score dropped in the sounds folder is offered beside the baked one
write /tmp/trk_home/.config/tracker/sounds/ping.score note 880 60 0.4
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Settings
wait 4
menu-pick Sounds
wait 12
expect-title Sounds
expect-sound-on beep
expect-sound-off window-zoom
expect-volume 80
note a checkbox applies at once and is saved -- there is no OK button
click 292 205
wait 5
expect-sound-off beep
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.beep off
click 292 305
wait 5
expect-sound-on window-zoom
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.window-zoom on
note Test sounds a moment that is off, without turning it on
click 682 330
wait 5
expect-sound window-activate
expect-sound-off window-activate
note pressing a row's sound name moves to the next file on offer, and
note plays it; past the last file it is the baked sound again
click 543 205
wait 8
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.beep.clip ping.score
expect-sound beep
click 543 205
wait 5
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.beep.clip
note a file from anywhere: the row's "..." puts the file panel up, and
note the file chosen is copied into the sounds folder and chosen there
write /tmp/trk_home/tick.score note 1200 40 0.4
click 642 205
wait 12
expect-title Open
click 338 200
wait 4
click 676 413
wait 12
expect-no-title Open
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.config/tracker/sounds/tick.score
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.beep.clip tick.score
expect-sound beep
note the volume is a slider: a press on the track puts the knob there
click 507 391
wait 5
expect-volume 50
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.volume 50
note and the knob follows the hand until it lets go
press 507 391
wait 2
move 600 391
wait 2
release 600 391
wait 5
expect-volume 77
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.volume 77
shot /tmp/trk_soundprefs.png
note Revert puts back what the window opened on; a default is not
note written down, so the file stops saying off rather than saying on
click 459 431
wait 5
expect-sound-on beep
expect-sound-off window-zoom
expect-volume 80
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.beep off
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings sound.beep.clip
quit
